                    <fillin characters="20"/>
                    .
                </md>
            </p>

            <p>
                If we now substitute <m>2k</m> for <m>m</m> in Equation
                <xref ref="eqn-n2even"/>, it follows that
                <md>
                    <fillin characters="20"/>
                    .
                </md>
                Dividing both sides by 2, we find that
                <md number="yes" xml:id="eqn-m2even">
                    <fillin characters="20"/>
                    .
                </md>
                Now Equation <xref ref="eqn-m2even"/> implies that <m>n^2</m> is
                even, and therefore by again <xref ref="lem-squareeven"/>,
                <m>n</m> must also be even.
                In particular, there exists some integer <m>p</m> such that
