        <activity workspace="1in">
            <p>
                We have now proved <m>\sqrt{2}</m> and <m>\sqrt{3}</m> are
                irrational.
                What other numbers can you prove are irrational using the same
                strategy and <xref ref="ch07-thm-primedivisor"/>?
                Can you prove <m>\sqrt{4}</m>, <m>\sqrt{5}</m>, and
                <m>\sqrt{6}</m> are all irrational?
            </p>
        </activity>
    </page>
</handout>